Call of Duty Modern Warfare in 2019  delivered a very different take on the  franchise introducing a year of  memorable moments like the nuke event  and Haunting of verdansk and kicked off  The free-to-play War Zone all while  Gathering a whole new Call of Duty fan  base with Modern Warfare 2 finally here  here's everything you need to know  Modern Warfare 2 picks up the plot three  years after the end of Modern Warfare  2019 when Captain Price formed Task  Force 141 and stopped a nuke launch in  verdance it's a sequel to the reboot  rather than a remake of the original  Modern Warfare 2 so we don't know  exactly how it will play out this time  fingers crossed that ghost doesn't get  absolutely fragged again though many  familiar faces return such as soap gas  ghost and price and there are some new  faces like Colonel Alejandro Vargas the  story involves the usual globetrotting  Special Operations you'd expect from  Call of Duty with a few new things to  consider many of the missions are  inspired by fan favorite Call of Duty  levels such as all gilded up and the  plot involves an American strike on a  high level 4 in general resulting in  that hostile country Contracting out  worldwide retaliation through the Los  Alamos drug cartel based in Mexico now  spec ops did not have a lot of details  until now with the Cod folks sending us  a bunch of Deeds on what you can expect  with the revamped game mode for example  additional special apps missions will  arrive as raids in season 1. there will  be three featured Missions at launch all  taking place in Al mazara the new war  zone map there's a bad situation which  is a stealth Mission you'll infiltrate a  town at night for Intel and evidence all  by alcatala there's vehicle Escape where  you'll navigate through winding streets  of a suburb trying to destroy Sam  turrets and Observatory defense a  survival mission where you defend the  observatory from increasingly difficult  waves of enemies trying to detonate  bombs operators can spend cash to get  items like killstreaks self-revive kits  and armor plates the operators in Spec  Ops will have access to a backpack as  well to store equipment and use one of  three kits similar to multiplayer perk  packages which are assault Medic or  engineer based each has their own play  Styles and sets of pros and cons as you  might image You Can level up these kits  by earning Stars through missions and  Mission related challenges Activision  strongly recommends you complete all  three missions with Max stars and to  have at least one kit leveled up to rank  5 before the raids are introduced in  season one which by the way raids being  part of spec ops are a direct  continuation of the campaign if you  decide a pre-order is right for you  players can get through the campaign a  week before the full launch guild-free  that they didn't fall behind in  multiplayer now alright we know you came  here for the guns so let's talk about  the new ways gunsmith Works weapons are  grouped into platforms now with the  receiver being the base of weapon trees  by leveling the receiver and adding  attachments within a single tree you can  build an SMG lmg battle rifle sniper  rifle Ursa monstrosity in between fair  warning the system was buried under a  few menus in the beta also keep in mind  that there are weapon specific  attachments and Universal attachments  Universal attachments only need to be  unlocked once and then they can be used  across multiple platforms eliminating  some repetitive grinding weapon specific  attachments are designed to make each  platform take on more unique roles  weapon blueprints also make a return or  players can buy weapon vaults which get  you every attachment and new cosmetic  appearance for a platform also you can  test your builds before going head to  head with other players best meta  leading creations at the offline firing  range which spots three firing Lanes a  climbing area and targets at different  distances oddly enough a lot of the new  gear does feel inspired by Rainbow Six  Siege like networked cameras drill  charges and decoys the important thing  to note is that the sandbox from 2019 is  still here with multiple test videos  already done by the community and us  check out our 18 things you didn't know  about Modern Warfare 2 multiplayer to  see what we mean now multiplayer has a  lot of customization options this time  around with PC sporting something along  like what 500 adjustments as well as  Ultra wide support console fans  including the previous gen will have a  fov slider this time around the game is  also cross play so it remains to be seen  if this gives PC players an advantage  now there's so much to talk about with  multiplayer this time around so let's  start with battle maps Modern Warfare  2019 leaned heavily into ground war and  large-scale 32-32 player battles return  the ground war is now only one of the  modes under battle maps in the beta we  already saw another Mode called Invasion  which pitted teams of players and Bots  against each other and by the time  Warzone launches you'll probably be  familiar with many of its locations like  serif Bay from the beta in fact battle  maps are intentionally meant to test  Warzone 2.0 points of interest ahead of  launch in battle maps every building can  be explored and several of the modes  involve Bots with developers suggesting  it's possible they can go up to 300 Bots  with a hundred players at some point the  vehicle roster has been expanded with  with multiple types of quads cars  armored trucks heavy and light tanks  helicopters and even boats the largest  transport the heavy Chopper has an  interior that players can walk around  and fight out of players have more  interactions with vehicles this time  around including the ability to lean out  destroy Parts such as blowout tires  which impacts handling and mantle or  hang off them another unique aspect of  Battle maps is how many of the new  tacticals lethals and field upgrades  were designed with combined arms and  Water Combat in mind many gadgets have  alternate modes and behaviors such as  how proximity mines float inflatable  decoys strike a swimming post DDOS and  shock sticks will shut down some  vehicles and trophy systems will stick  to vehicles in order to stop incoming  projectiles on the Move core maps  consist of tighter 6v6 engagements but  despite being described as more  straightforward we found they were still  fairly large in the beta with a lot of  different routes through them and plenty  of vertical space core maps sport a few  competitive no respawn modes such as  knockout where teams need to hold a bag  for 60 seconds or eliminate the enemy  team to win there's also prisoner rescue  where one team scores points by rescuing  two hostages while the other team tries  to eliminate them the usual suspects  also return here like domination TDM and  hardpoint third person mode is there for  many of these modes and adds some flavor  like shoulder swapping but it doesn't  significantly change how the rounds play  out because players can still go to  first person when aiming down sights now  Warzone 2.0 is free to play and releases  on November 16th a few weeks after the  campaign in multiplayer almazra runs on  the same engine and mechanics as  multiplayer and is a complete reboot  with the first war zone remaining its  own experience that also means that your  previous war zone skins guns and  purchases won't carry over almazara is  the biggest Call of Duty map in the  franchise with 18 point points of  interest and because of that Sports a  new multi-circle close mechanic with  players needing to win within several  individual circles before they close  down and they all fight in the final  Circle it can support up to 150 players  with additional AI Loadout drops have  been replaced by the shop which are buy  stations where you can buy more stuff  than the first war zone which includes  weapons and your own gunsmith Creations  when purchased they replace your entire  looted inventory and this also continues  to be where you buy Squad mates back AI  is a big part of Modern Warfare 2 and  Warzone features with both Bots  scattered around the map and strongholds  which are areas full of tougher AI  combatants guarding higher tier loot  Bots will not chase you though so you  can fight or ignore them if you die  during a match you will go to the new  Gulag which is modeled much closer to  the previous gunfight Mode in Modern  Warfare 2019 than the current War zones  Gulag teams of two start with nothing  and loot the area before either winning  to gain a second chance back to the war  zone map or getting knocked out of the  round the gulag also has a tough AI boss  called the Jailer who can show up and if  both teams cooperate to take them down  all that means that both teams can go  back to the war zone match players keep  any gear found in the gulag so they  don't drop back onto the main map a  Sitting Duck now not a lot has been said  about DMZ yet it's a mysterious mode  that we know to be a extraction mode and  it seems to have a gear collection  mechanic and rumors still have it pegged  as a potential escape from tarkov style  freeform mode but we'll have to wait and  see very little has been confirmed about  Modern Warfare 2 post launch Warzone of  course will have a number of Seasons as  expected Activision has been rumored to  be looking into moving away from the  yearly Call of Duty cycle which would  mean more than a year of DLC for Modern  Warfare 2 but only if that winds up  being true they have said that premium  Call of Duty content will come out in  2023 so we just don't know yet other  Rumors in speculation and to add older  Modern Warfare 2 maps being released  post-launch but none of this is  confirmed the dev blog described it as a  years-long journey to come with our  players now Modern Warfare 2 and Warzone  are multi-platform releases including  PS4 PS5 Xbox One Xbox series X and S and  PC PC including steam by the way it  supports cross play and cross  progression now this time around there  is a multi-week launch with Early Access  campaign on October 20th a full launch  on October 28th a war zone 2.0 and DMZ  launch on November 16th and raids are  coming with season 1 starting December  14th that was an intense amount of  information so most importantly don't  forget to have fun and stick around for  upcoming reviews test videos and guides  keep an eye out for videos from myself  and our other Cod experts on staff Aaron  Samson and Decker I'm David and I'll see  you all out there in battle thanks for  watching
 

